data.comment:
Implementation complete — see commits 90b31939, 336bb8dd, a2180b8d on dev (branch wl-AH-0MW2DC20A007TAVY-dev-telemetry-serialisation-costs-5-of-j).

**AC1 — no serialise+redact of a payload that will be discarded.** The whole-file run-end upload now refuses an over-cap run from the sink's metered byte count before it reads the buffer: `readByteLength()` (O(1), metered per line for the retention cap) feeds `checkDevUploadSizeFromBytes(bytes, cap)` in `src/telemetry/devUpload.ts`, and `readSink` is never called. Tests on that seam: 'refuses an over-cap run from its byte count without reading the buffer' (asserts `readSink` not called) and the `checkDevUploadSizeFromBytes` unit tests, which also pin that it never contradicts the full-body guard.

**AC2 — redaction unchanged.** Every payload still passes through `sanitiseTelemetryValue` at the recorder boundary; the change only memoises the per-key verdict and the email scan behind bounded caches (`REDACTION_CACHE_LIMIT`), with tests proving identical output on repeat calls and bounded growth. All existing redaction tests pass unchanged, plus the recorder's 'redacts sensitive payload fields before they reach a sink'.

**AC3 — measured (paired, 3 interleaved runs per arm).** 60 s PlayScene late-game demo (`--setup '{"demo":true,"seed":1,"startLevel":10}'`), base ddb59ee4 vs a2180b8d, host load 9.1–12.1 vs 10.4–12.3, enemy peak 1224–1536 in both arms:
- all `src/telemetry/*` + `botSnapshot` self time: **10.04 % → 6.54 % of JS**, **0.520 % → 0.320 % of the window**, **316.6 ms → 198.4 ms** (−38 %);
- `sanitise`+`sanitiseObject`: 3.60 % / 115.4 ms → 2.47 % / 74.4 ms;
- `deepFreeze`: 1.82 % / 60.1 ms → 1.08 % / 32.9 ms (telemetry snapshot no longer frozen);
- `devUploadMessageBytes` (per-part `JSON.stringify` escaping): 1.31 % / 43.3 ms → below the profile cut;
- `write`: 0.83 % / 26.9 ms → 0.69 % / 20.5 ms;
- FPS/frame time unchanged (median 52.3 FPS both arms, p50 16.7 ms).
Recorded in `docs/PERFORMANCE.md` § 'Dev telemetry recorder cost' and hotspot row #10; the cap behaviour is documented in `docs/TELEMETRY.md`.

**AC4 — full suite green**: the finish gate's pre-lock dev-push full-suite verdict for tree 226cddde was green (executed, 208.5 s), and changed-scope was green (1040 tests).

Notes / decisions:
- A hand-written ASCII fast path for `utf8ByteLength` was implemented, measured (58 ms vs 7.6 ms for the native encoder in a 60 s window) and **reverted**; the shared helper keeps one module-scoped `TextEncoder` instead. Documented so it is not re-attempted.
- The streaming part sender now uses a sound JSON-text escaping bound (at most 2× — a control character never appears raw in `JSON.stringify` output) instead of escaping every ~2 MiB window to measure it; anything the bound does not clear is still measured exactly.
- A record-time latch that would have stopped sanitising a run once it passed the cap was **rejected**: with the streaming path active a long run *is* delivered in bounded windows, so truncating would silently lose telemetry. Only the refuse-to-serialise path (which loses nothing) was implemented.
